----------
> Alarms
> Is there any way from an OPL program of interfacing the standard Psion 
> alarms i.e. to set one from another application ?

If you want to set an alarm from within an OPL program, the following 
code ought to do you nicely:

PROC alm:
LOCAL h%,a&(2),a$(64),b$(65),d&,t&,t2&,a%,r%,s%
r%=IOOPEN(h%,"ALM:",0)
IF r%<0 :RAISE r% :ENDIF
d&=DAYS(DAY,MONTH,YEAR) REM today
t&=DATETOSECS(1970,1,1,HOUR,MINUTE,0)
DINIT "Set alarm"
DTIME t&,"Time",0,0,DATETOSECS(1970,1,1,23,59,59)
DDATE d&,"Date",d&,DAYS(31,12,2049)
DTIME t2&,"Alarm advance time",2,0,86399
DEDIT a$,"Message"
IF DIALOG
        a&(2)=86400*(d&-25567)+t&
        a&(1)=a&(2)-t2&
        b$=a$+CHR$(0)
        a%=ADDR(b$)
        r%=IOA(h%,2,s%,a&(),#a%+1)
        IF r%<0 :RAISE r% :ENDIF
ENDIF
r%=IOCLOSE(h%)
IF r%<0 :RAISE r% :ENDIF
ENDP

Admiration and respect to Ali Manson for this code.

Anthea



